  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "A box contains twenty critters, and each is either a spider or a fly. If they have 138 legs in total, then how many spiders and how many flies are in the box?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "9 spiders and 11 flies.",
      "worked": "Let $s$ be the number of spiders and $f$ the number of flies. Spiders have eight legs and flies have six legs.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}s+f&=20 &&(1)\\\\8s+6f&=138 &&(2)\\\\6s+6f&=120 &&6\\times(1)\\\\2s&=18 &&(2)-6\\times(1)\\\\s&=9\\\\9+f&=20\\\\f&=11\\end{align*}$$\n\nThere are 9 spiders and 11 flies. Check: $9+11=20$ and $8(9)+6(11)=138$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 84
  },
